  "estimatedMinutes": null,
  "statement": "Determine the number of integers \\(2 \\leq n \\leq 2016\\) such that \\(n^{n}-1\\) is divisible by \\(2,3,5,7\\).",
  "answerChoices": [],
  "answer": {
    "letter": null,
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-guts-2016-p16.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Answer: 9\nOnly \\(n \\equiv 1(\\bmod 210)\\) work. Proof: we require \\(\\operatorname{gcd}(n, 210)=1\\). Note that \\(\\forall p \\leq 7\\) the order of \\(n\\) \\((\\bmod p)\\) divides \\(p-1\\), hence is relatively prime to any \\(p \\leq 7\\). So \\(n^{n} \\equiv 1(\\bmod p) \\Longleftrightarrow n \\equiv 1(\\bmod p)\\) for each of these \\(p\\).",
